{
 "_note": [
  "Generic money phrases, per language, for the country-plus-topic query.",
  "",
  "WHY THIS EXISTS. The per-currency query in listen_queries.py only matches",
  "the currency's NAME or CODE, so it misses everyone who talks about a",
  "country's money without naming it - 'Nigeria's currency is collapsing',",
  "'Egypt devaluation incoming'. Those are the same conversation and they",
  "carry no currency name at all.",
  "",
  "HOW IT IS USED. Country AND one-of-these, not OR'd into the currency",
  "query:",
  "    Nigeria (\"exchange rate\" OR forex OR devaluation OR currency)",
  "Words sitting next to each other AND in X search, so the tweet must",
  "mention the country AND at least one money phrase. 'currency' alone would",
  "be hopeless noise; anchored to a country it is precise.",
  "",
  "NO TRANSLATION HAPPENS. X matches literal text - searching 'currency'",
  "never matches 'monnaie'. Every language needs its phrases written out.",
  "English is always included alongside the local set, because plenty of",
  "people in Lagos, Karachi and Manila discuss their own currency in",
  "English.",
  "",
  "",
  "CONFIDENCE is the author's and is honest: high / medium / low. A wrong",
  "phrase returns zero, which reads exactly like a quiet market. Treat a",
  "zero from a low-confidence language as unmeasured, not as evidence.",
  "",
  "X NORMALISES, VERIFIED 2026-08-13 by searching both forms and comparing",
  "results. Accents fold (dolar finds dólar and vice versa) and plurals stem",
  "(pesos finds peso). So write ONE form - the accented singular - and do",
  "not add variants. Five redundant plurals were removed after this test.",
  "Irregular plurals that are not a simple -s (meticais, guaraníes) are kept",
  "because stemming was not verified for those, and a bare form that differs",
  "from a phrase already listed (colones against 'colón costarricense') is",
  "kept because a phrase never matches a bare word."
 ],
